00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:16.560
On November 8th, 2016 at 8:15 PM, TVs across
India flickered in unison.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.779
Dramas, cricket matches, and game shows were
all replaced with the face of Prime Minister

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:23.210
Modi.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.810
In this unscheduled, surprise address, he
announced the 500 and 1,000 rupee banknotes

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:36.180
- worth about 7 and 14 US Dollars, respectively
- would soon lose their status as legal tender.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.269
Without any monetary value, they would become
nothing but pieces of paper, useless for any

00:00:41.269 --> 00:00:42.989
and all transactions.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:49.530
”Soon” meant in 3 hours and 45 minutes
- effective immediately at midnight.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:56.920
And those 500 and 1,000 rupee bills constituted
no less than 86% of all cash in circulation.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:03.570
It was as if the U.S. president suddenly announced
all 10, and $20 bills were worthless,

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.890
only with a population 4 times bigger and
far more reliant on cash.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:14.900
The next few months were the result of a fascinating,
unintended experiment, as 1.3 billion people

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:20.300
scrambled to replace their cash, the government
rushed to print new bills, and dozens of people

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.860
died in the process.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.980
India runs on cash.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:32.420
It’s estimated that, measured by volume,
90-98% of all transactions in the country

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.270
involve physical currency.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:40.630
and 85% of workers are paid in cash, while
only about half the population owns a bank

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:41.630
account.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:47.540
These are optimal conditions for tax theft,
making it extremely easy and extremely common

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:53.230
for earnings to go unreported, and, thus,
unknown and untracked by the government.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:59.710
The informal, underground economy makes up
something like 25 to 40% of the nation’s

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:00.710
GDP.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:05.260
While salaried workers have taxes automatically
withheld from their paychecks, they represent

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.090
only a tenth of all organized workers.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:13.790
Farmers, meanwhile, who make up about half
the nation’s workforce, are largely exempt

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:19.430
- protected from politicians by their large
voting power, not unlike seniors in the United

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.430
States.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:26.730
In 2016, only 37 million Indians filed tax
returns, 10 million of which were exempt,

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:31.950
leaving only a tiny 27 million payers in a
country of 1.3 billion.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:37.300
Modi’s solution was simple: force everyone
to report their earnings.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:43.230
From November 9th, Indians had until December
30th to take their 500 and 1,000 rupee notes

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.230
to the bank.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:49.360
There, they could be deposited for their full
value, or exchanged for other notes at the

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:56.410
counter, for a maximum of 4,000 rupees per
person per day, later increased to 4,500 and

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.750
then reduced to 2,000.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:04.569
Tax avoiders, big and small, now had no choice
but to declare their wealth or lose it all

00:03:04.569 --> 00:03:06.060
come January.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.590
Any strange, large deposits without explanatory
paperwork would be an instant red flag for

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:12.819
the government.

00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:15.190
But here’s where everything went wrong:

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:20.630
The central bank couldn’t prepare millions
of new, replacement banknotes in secret.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.700
Printing them in advance would therefore attract
attention, potentially cause chaos, and alert

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.930
the very criminals the policy was meant to
target.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:33.691
For this reason, the Reserve Bank could only
start printing the new 500 and 2,000 rupee

00:03:33.691 --> 00:03:38.760
notes after the announcement - leaving it
with just under 4 hours to reprint the vast

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.000
majority of the second-most populous nation’s
currency.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.790
Clearly, it was an impossible task.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:50.020
Now, having to bring cash to deposit or exchange
would’ve been disruptive enough for many

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.250
Indians,

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:56.340
but because the new banknotes were in such
short supply, long lines formed outside banks

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.790
and ATMs for months.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:04.410
On top of that, the replacement bills were
slightly smaller, requiring ATMs to be retrofitted

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.470
to use them.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:11.210
There were lawsuits, strikes, and protests
against what many saw as an unreasonable interference

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.620
by the government in daily life.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:18.539
And despite all that, there’s good reason
to be skeptical the policy achieved its intended

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:19.539
effects.

00:04:19.539 --> 00:04:22.340
Broadly speaking, there were two goals of
demonetization:

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.139
First, to weaken terrorist funding,

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:28.460
and second, to target the informal, black
economy.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.699
Both of which are hard to measure.

00:04:30.699 --> 00:04:35.719
Whether terrorist groups suffered any significant
losses as a result of demonetization, no one

00:04:35.719 --> 00:04:37.380
knows with certainty.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:42.330
And the black market is problematic precisely
because it can’t be measured.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:48.520
What we do know, according to the Reserve
Bank of India itself, is that 99.3% of the

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.490
demonetized notes were later returned.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:56.550
In other words, the policy removed only a
tiny amount of money from circulation.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:05:02.190
Experts largely agree black money is mostly
stored in the form of gold, silver, real estate,

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:07.370
and overseas bank accounts, not bills worth
7 or 14 US Dollars each.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:13.490
It’s true that demonetization added a record
9 million new taxpayers, but the mass disruption

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:20.169
it caused also removed nearly the same amount
- 8.8 million people stopped paying that year,

00:05:20.169 --> 00:05:22.599
likely as a result of lost income.

00:05:22.599 --> 00:05:27.999
And while digital payments experienced a significant
spike in usage, there was no lasting effect

00:05:27.999 --> 00:05:30.879
after the new banknotes were fully distributed.

00:05:30.879 --> 00:05:35.849
Three years later, the only certain outcome
of demonetization was the immediate chaos

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:41.599
it created across the nation: Hours wasted
at the bank, financial uncertainty for those

00:05:41.599 --> 00:05:46.139
most vulnerable, lost wages, and at least
several innocent lives.

00:05:46.139 --> 00:05:51.339
Worse, it came out of nowhere, not as a response
to inflation or unrest.

00:05:51.339 --> 00:05:57.749
So, why, then, given all that we now know,
is the policy still so popular in India, among

00:05:57.749 --> 00:06:00.719
those who personally paid its costs?

00:06:00.719 --> 00:06:06.150
Like Xi Jinping’s consolidation of power
in China, Modi successfully sold a story of

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:12.210
unfairness, of targeting corruption and criminals,
to ultimately gain political support.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:18.930
Soon after, Modi’s party won the 2017 elections
of its 200-million person, most populous state

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:23.869
in India, thanks, in part, to the popular
belief that demonetization was a collective

00:06:23.869 --> 00:06:27.830
sacrifice necessary to make the rich pay their
fair share.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:32.650
Anyone who protested the policy could easily
be labeled as a criminal trying to hide black

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.650
money.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:38.710
Rather than turning the population against
the government, demonetization enlisted it,

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:42.729
making people feel they were personally doing
their part to help fight crime.

00:06:42.729 --> 00:06:48.689
Modi’s party could’ve passed just as effective
but less disruptive laws targeting black money

00:06:48.689 --> 00:06:50.749
and explained them to gain support.

00:06:50.749 --> 00:06:57.599
Instead, he knew the most effective way to
convey information is by showing people, firsthand.

00:06:57.599 --> 00:07:02.960
Demonetization achieved its real goal of driving
political support by making a faraway, abstract

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.839
concept tangible and interactive.

